      "side": 1,
      "message": "The TFS protocols involve fragmentation, aggregation, and reassembly for every tunneled packet, so we did a lot of buffer chain debugging, which pcap would not address. Although omitting this tracing obviously won\u0027t break the implementation, we think this tracing would be generally useful in vpp.\n\nHowever, I will be doing some performance experiments with various approaches to collating the packets (e.g., copying vs. chaining) so I am happy to defer consideration of this change until afterward.\n\nDo you have any opinions in light of the above? Thanks",
